---
import ExplainerLayout from "../../layouts/ExplainerLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../../components/explainer/Hero.astro";
import Aside from "../../components/explainer/Aside.astro";
import Figure from "../../components/explainer/Figure.astro";
import ControlRange from "../../components/explainer/ControlRange.astro";
import ControlSelect from "../../components/explainer/ControlSelect.astro";
import NextCards from "../../components/explainer/NextCards.astro";
---

<ExplainerLayout title="Subspace Geometry" breadcrumb="Subspace Geometry" section="interpretability-methods">
<Hero title="Subspace Geometry" subtitle="PCA, principal angles, Procrustes fits, and relative representations explain how two nearly different-looking bases can still carry the same structure." />

<p>
Representation papers often compare spaces rather than single neurons. A probe
may work after projecting to the top PCA components; two models may have nearly
orthogonal principal bases; an affine map may still align their examples. The
geometry is easier to see as a moving point cloud than as a table of cosines.
</p>

<p class="schematic-note">The figures on this page are schematic: the angles and transfer scores illustrate the geometry, not measured results from a specific model.</p>

<Figure title="Figure 1 · Drag or scrub the rotation and watch the principal angle open" canvasId="subspace-cloud-canvas" width="760" height="430" readoutId="subspace-cloud-readout">
<Fragment slot="controls">
  <ControlRange id="subspace-angle" label="rotation" valueId="subspace-angle-v" min="0" max="89" step="1" value="54" />
</Fragment>
</Figure>

<h2>1. PCA chooses a subspace, not a mechanism</h2>

<p>
PCA finds directions of high variance. In probe transfer work, the top-k
subspace can be a useful compression before fitting an alignment map. That does
not mean variance caused the feature. It means the feature was readable after a
particular low-rank projection.
</p>

<p>
Principal angles summarize how two subspaces sit relative to one another. Small
angles mean the planes overlap; angles near 90 degrees mean the bases can look
almost orthogonal. But a bad-looking basis comparison is not the same as a failed
example alignment.
</p>

<Figure title="Figure 2 · Procrustes rotation versus affine fit" canvasId="subspace-fit-canvas" width="760" height="390" readoutId="subspace-fit-readout">
<Fragment slot="controls">
  <ControlSelect id="subspace-fit-mode" label="alignment" valueId="subspace-fit-mode-v" options={[
    { value: "procrustes", label: "rotation-only", selected: true },
    { value: "affine", label: "affine map" },
  ]} />
  <ControlRange id="subspace-fit-step" label="fit progress" valueId="subspace-fit-step-v" min="0" max="1" step="0.05" value="0.55" />
  <button class="play-btn" data-play-target="subspace-fit-step" data-play-from="0" data-play-to="1" data-play-duration="1700" aria-label="Play the Procrustes fit from start to converged">▶ Play fit</button>
</Fragment>
</Figure>

<h2>2. Alignment maps answer a different question</h2>

<p>
Procrustes alignment rotates one centered cloud toward another while preserving
distances. An affine fit can also stretch, shear, and translate. If Procrustes
fails but affine succeeds, the result says the examples share a recoverable
coordinate relationship, not that the two models used identical geometry.
</p>

<Aside>
  <strong>Near-orthogonal bases can still transfer.</strong> A top PCA basis can
  point almost nowhere near another top PCA basis while the examples themselves
  remain alignable after an affine map. The important question is whether the
  selected subspace keeps task-relevant neighborhoods and directions.
</Aside>

<Figure title="Figure 3 · Subspace selection beats rank alone" canvasId="subspace-counter-canvas" width="760" height="350" readoutId="subspace-counter-readout">
<Fragment slot="controls">
  <ControlRange id="subspace-counter-angle" label="basis angle" valueId="subspace-counter-angle-v" min="70" max="89" step="1" value="87" />
</Fragment>
</Figure>

<h2>3. Relative representations use anchors</h2>

<p>
Absolute coordinates are fragile. Rotate every point and a coordinate probe has
to relearn its weights. Distances or cosines to anchor examples can stay stable
under the same rotation, giving a relative representation that survives changes
of basis.
</p>

<Figure title="Figure 4 · Rotate coordinates; anchor signatures stay fixed" canvasId="subspace-anchor-canvas" width="760" height="360" readoutId="subspace-anchor-readout">
<Fragment slot="controls">
  <ControlRange id="subspace-anchor-rotation" label="coordinate rotation" valueId="subspace-anchor-rotation-v" min="0" max="180" step="5" value="45" />
</Fragment>
</Figure>

<div class="source-list">
  <strong>Related pages</strong>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/ml/structural-probes/">Dependency Trees & Structural Probes</a> for the tree-distance probe that often gets aligned across models.</li>
    <li><a href="/ml/interchange-interventions/">Interchange Interventions & DAS</a> for learned rotations used as causal interventions.</li>
    <li><a href="/ml/residual-stream-directions/">Residual Stream & Directions</a> for the local "feature as direction" approximation.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<NextCards cards={[
  { href: "/ml/structural-probes/", tag: "Application", title: "Structural Probes", role: "Where cross-model alignment pressure appears." },
  { href: "/ml/interchange-interventions/", tag: "Method", title: "Interchange Interventions", role: "How trained low-rank slices become causal tests." },
]} />

<script is:inline>
  (() => {
    const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
    const fmt = (x) => `${Math.round(x)}°`;
    const pts = [
      [-1.2, -0.4, 0.15], [-0.8, 0.2, -0.35], [-0.45, -0.6, 0.42], [-0.2, 0.5, 0.28], [0.35, -0.1, -0.2],
      [0.65, 0.55, 0.5], [0.95, -0.5, -0.45], [1.25, 0.15, 0.08], [0.1, 0.95, -0.25], [-1.05, 0.75, 0.36],
    ];
    const anchors = [[-1.05, 0.75, 0.36], [0.95, -0.5, -0.45], [0.1, 0.95, -0.25]];

    function env(id, logicalW, logicalH) {
      const canvas = $(id);
      if (!canvas) return null;
      const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
      const dpr = Math.max(1, window.devicePixelRatio || 1);
      const cssW = rect.width || logicalW;
      const cssH = rect.height || logicalH;
      canvas.width = Math.round(cssW * dpr);
      canvas.height = Math.round(cssH * dpr);
      const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
      ctx.setTransform((cssW / logicalW) * dpr, 0, 0, (cssH / logicalH) * dpr, 0, 0);
      return { ctx, w: logicalW, h: logicalH };
    }
    function rot(p, deg) {
      const a = (deg * Math.PI) / 180;
      const x = p[0] * Math.cos(a) - p[2] * Math.sin(a);
      const z = p[0] * Math.sin(a) + p[2] * Math.cos(a);
      const b = a * 0.45;
      return [x, p[1] * Math.cos(b) - z * Math.sin(b), p[1] * Math.sin(b) + z * Math.cos(b)];
    }
    function xy(p, cx, cy, s = 88) {
      const z = p[2] || 0;
      return [cx + p[0] * s + z * 22, cy - p[1] * s + z * 10];
    }
    function point(ctx, p, cx, cy, color, r = 4.5) {
      const z = p[2] || 0;
      const [x, y] = xy(p, cx, cy);
      ctx.fillStyle = color;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.72 + Math.max(-0.4, Math.min(0.4, z)) * 0.4;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(x, y, r + z * 1.2, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
    }
    function axes(ctx, cx, cy, angle, color, len = 120) {
      const a = (angle * Math.PI) / 180;
      ctx.strokeStyle = color;
      ctx.lineWidth = 3;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(cx - Math.cos(a) * len, cy + Math.sin(a) * len);
      ctx.lineTo(cx + Math.cos(a) * len, cy - Math.sin(a) * len);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.45;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(cx - Math.cos(a + Math.PI / 2) * len * 0.58, cy + Math.sin(a + Math.PI / 2) * len * 0.58);
      ctx.lineTo(cx + Math.cos(a + Math.PI / 2) * len * 0.58, cy - Math.sin(a + Math.PI / 2) * len * 0.58);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
    }

    function drawCloud() {
      const out = env("subspace-cloud-canvas", 760, 430);
      if (!out) return;
      const { ctx } = out;
      const angle = Number($("subspace-angle")?.value || 54);
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, 760, 430);
      ctx.fillStyle = "#0f172a";
      ctx.font = "700 18px system-ui";
      ctx.fillText("Same examples, different basis", 42, 42);
      ctx.fillStyle = "#64748b";
      ctx.font = "13px system-ui";
      ctx.fillText("The principal plane turns as the representation basis turns.", 42, 64);
      axes(ctx, 230, 230, 0, "#0ea5e9");
      axes(ctx, 530, 230, angle, "#be123c");
      pts.forEach((p) => point(ctx, p, 230, 230, "#0ea5e9"));
      pts.map((p) => rot(p, angle)).forEach((p) => point(ctx, p, 530, 230, "#be123c"));
      ctx.fillStyle = "#111827";
      ctx.font = "700 14px system-ui";
      ctx.fillText("model A PCA plane", 155, 382);
      ctx.fillText("model B PCA plane", 455, 382);
      const cos = Math.cos((angle * Math.PI) / 180);
      $("subspace-cloud-readout") && ($("subspace-cloud-readout").textContent = `Principal angle between the two top planes ${fmt(angle)}; principal cosine ${cos.toFixed(2)}. Rank selection is explored separately in Figure 3.`);
      $("subspace-angle-v") && ($("subspace-angle-v").textContent = fmt(angle));
    }

    function drawFit() {
      const out = env("subspace-fit-canvas", 760, 390);
      if (!out) return;
      const { ctx } = out;
      const mode = $("subspace-fit-mode")?.value || "procrustes";
      const step = Number($("subspace-fit-step")?.value || 0.55);
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, 760, 390);
      ctx.fillStyle = "#0f172a";
      ctx.font = "700 18px system-ui";
      ctx.fillText("Move source points toward the target cloud", 44, 42);
      const target = pts.map((p) => [p[0] * 1.05 + 0.15, p[1] * 0.9 - 0.05]);
      const start = pts.map((p) => rot([p[0] * 1.35 - 0.4, p[1] * 0.65 + 0.25], 48));
      const mapped = start.map((p, i) => {
        const t = target[i];
        const affineBoost = mode === "affine" ? 1 : 0.62;
        return [p[0] + (t[0] - p[0]) * step * affineBoost, p[1] + (t[1] - p[1]) * step * affineBoost];
      });
      target.forEach((p) => point(ctx, p, 380, 210, "#0ea5e9", 5));
      mapped.forEach((p, i) => {
        point(ctx, p, 380, 210, mode === "affine" ? "#be123c" : "#f97316", 4.5);
        const [x1, y1] = xy(p, 380, 210);
        const [x2, y2] = xy(target[i], 380, 210);
        ctx.strokeStyle = "#cbd5e1";
        ctx.lineWidth = 1;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.moveTo(x1, y1);
        ctx.lineTo(x2, y2);
        ctx.stroke();
      });
      const residual = mode === "affine" ? 0.36 * (1 - step) : 0.26 + 0.46 * (1 - step);
      $("subspace-fit-readout") && ($("subspace-fit-readout").textContent = `${mode === "affine" ? "Affine" : "Rotation-only"} fit residual ${(residual).toFixed(2)}: lower is better, but the allowed map changes the claim.`);
      $("subspace-fit-mode-v") && ($("subspace-fit-mode-v").textContent = $("subspace-fit-mode").selectedOptions[0].textContent);
      $("subspace-fit-step-v") && ($("subspace-fit-step-v").textContent = `${Math.round(step * 100)}%`);
    }

    function drawCounter() {
      const out = env("subspace-counter-canvas", 760, 350);
      if (!out) return;
      const { ctx } = out;
      const angle = Number($("subspace-counter-angle")?.value || 87);
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, 760, 350);
      ctx.fillStyle = "#0f172a";
      ctx.font = "700 18px system-ui";
      ctx.fillText("Same rank, same basis angle, different information", 42, 42);
      const selected = 0.86 - (angle - 70) * 0.006;
      const random = 0.34 - (angle - 70) * 0.003;
      function panel(x, label, score, color) {
        ctx.fillStyle = "#fff";
        ctx.strokeStyle = "#d7dde8";
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.roundRect(x, 82, 300, 210, 12);
        ctx.fill();
        ctx.stroke();
        axes(ctx, x + 150, 170, angle, color, 82);
        pts.slice(0, 7).forEach((p) => point(ctx, rot(p, angle), x + 150, 170, color, 4));
        ctx.fillStyle = "#111827";
        ctx.font = "700 14px system-ui";
        ctx.fillText(label, x + 24, 116);
        ctx.fillStyle = "#f1f5f9";
        ctx.fillRect(x + 24, 250, 220, 18);
        ctx.fillStyle = color;
        ctx.fillRect(x + 24, 250, 220 * score, 18);
        ctx.fillStyle = "#475569";
        ctx.font = "12px system-ui";
        ctx.fillText(`transfer ${(score * 100).toFixed(0)}%`, x + 252, 264);
      }
      panel(66, "selected PCA subspace", selected, "#be123c");
      panel(394, "random rank-matched subspace", random, "#94a3b8");
      $("subspace-counter-readout") && ($("subspace-counter-readout").textContent = `Both panels use a ${fmt(angle)} basis angle; selected subspaces preserve neighborhoods that random rank alone does not.`);
      $("subspace-counter-angle-v") && ($("subspace-counter-angle-v").textContent = fmt(angle));
    }

    function drawAnchor() {
      const out = env("subspace-anchor-canvas", 760, 360);
      if (!out) return;
      const { ctx } = out;
      const angle = Number($("subspace-anchor-rotation")?.value || 45);
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, 760, 360);
      ctx.fillStyle = "#0f172a";
      ctx.font = "700 18px system-ui";
      ctx.fillText("Coordinates change; anchor distances do not", 42, 42);
      const query = [0.35, -0.1, -0.2];
      const rq = rot(query, angle);
      const rAnchors = anchors.map((p) => rot(p, angle));
      anchors.forEach((p, i) => point(ctx, p, 210, 195, ["#0ea5e9", "#be123c", "#f97316"][i], 7));
      point(ctx, query, 210, 195, "#111827", 6);
      rAnchors.forEach((p, i) => point(ctx, p, 510, 195, ["#0ea5e9", "#be123c", "#f97316"][i], 7));
      point(ctx, rq, 510, 195, "#111827", 6);
      ctx.fillStyle = "#475569";
      ctx.font = "13px system-ui";
      ctx.fillText("absolute coordinates", 152, 320);
      ctx.fillText("after rotation", 468, 320);
      const sig = anchors.map((a) => Math.hypot(a[0] - query[0], a[1] - query[1], a[2] - query[2]).toFixed(2)).join(", ");
      $("subspace-anchor-readout") && ($("subspace-anchor-readout").textContent = `Anchor signature [${sig}] is unchanged after a ${fmt(angle)} coordinate rotation.`);
      $("subspace-anchor-rotation-v") && ($("subspace-anchor-rotation-v").textContent = fmt(angle));
    }

    let draggingCloud = false;
    let lastX = 0;
    const cloudCanvas = $("subspace-cloud-canvas");
    cloudCanvas?.addEventListener("pointerdown", (event) => {
      draggingCloud = true;
      lastX = event.clientX;
      cloudCanvas.setPointerCapture(event.pointerId);
    });
    cloudCanvas?.addEventListener("pointermove", (event) => {
      if (!draggingCloud) return;
      const input = $("subspace-angle");
      if (!input) return;
      const next = Math.max(0, Math.min(89, Number(input.value) + (event.clientX - lastX) * 0.35));
      input.value = String(next.toFixed(0));
      lastX = event.clientX;
      drawCloud();
    });
    cloudCanvas?.addEventListener("pointerup", () => { draggingCloud = false; });
    cloudCanvas?.addEventListener("pointercancel", () => { draggingCloud = false; });
    $("subspace-angle")?.addEventListener("input", drawCloud);
    ["subspace-fit-mode", "subspace-fit-step"].forEach((id) => $(id)?.addEventListener("input", drawFit));
    $("subspace-counter-angle")?.addEventListener("input", drawCounter);
    $("subspace-anchor-rotation")?.addEventListener("input", drawAnchor);
    window.addEventListener("resize", () => { drawCloud(); drawFit(); drawCounter(); drawAnchor(); });
    drawCloud();
    drawFit();
    drawCounter();
    drawAnchor();
  })();
</script>
<script is:inline src="/ml/mech-interp/mech-interp.js"></script>
</ExplainerLayout>
